1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,280
Ollie: The rain stopped! Everything is shiny, Pip!

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,820
Pip: Ollie, look up. Look up!

3
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:13,760
Ollie: A rainbow! It's so big and so bright!

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,890
Ollie: Where does a rainbow come from?

5
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,880
Ollie: Let's find out!

6
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:57,690
Pip: Maybe the sky painted it.

7
00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,710
Ollie: With what? Sky paint?

8
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:05,060
Pip: Maybe it fell off a very big butterfly.

9
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:16,620
Gus: Easy! The rainbow is a prize, and I'm getting it!

10
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:20,050
Ollie: A prize for what?

11
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:26,080
Gus: For whoever gets to the end first. And that's me!

12
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:30,410
Ollie: I'll race you, Gus! Follow me!

13
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:36,970
Pip: Ollie, I have an idea! Ollie? Please stop!

14
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:43,020
Ollie: Sorry, Pip. I ran before I listened. What's your idea?

15
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:49,910
Pip: The rain stopped and the sun came out. Maybe they go together.

16
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:53,810
Gus: Too slow! I've got a faster way!

17
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:59,700
Pip: Gus, your faster ways always go wrong.

18
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,310
Gus: Not this time! I'll run to the end and grab the rainbow!

19
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:06,600
Ollie: Can you grab a rainbow?

20
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,500
Gus: Watch me! I'll put it in my hat!

21
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,180
Pip: What if we try it the careful way?

22
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:20,650
Ollie: Let's watch Gus first. Then we ask Gran Mari.

23
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:30,200
Gus: Hey! Stay still, rainbow!

24
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:44,240
Gus: There it is! It came down all by itself!

25
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:48,820
Ollie: Gus, that's a different rainbow.

26
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:54,140
Gus: It's mine now! I caught it!

27
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,550
Gus: My rainbow. Nobody else gets to look.

28
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,710
Bean: Share?

29
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,840
Gus: Uh oh. Where did it go?

30
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:15,210
Pip: Did you lose it, Gus?

31
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:20,550
Gus: No! It's just sleeping. Rainbows sleep a lot.

32
00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:24,200
Ollie: Rainbows sleep?

33
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:28,240
Gus: It was tiny anyway. Hardly a rainbow at all!

34
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:38,290
Ollie: We need help. Let's ask Gran Mari.

35
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:50,570
Gran Mari: Well now, a seagull with a tiny hat and an otter with a big question. What's all this?

36
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:55,110
Ollie: Gran Mari, where does a rainbow come from?

37
00:03:56,610 --> 00:04:06,210
Gran Mari: Oh, that is a good question, Ollie. Let's find out together.

38
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:16,870
Gran Mari: Never look right at the sun, little one. We look at the wall instead.

39
00:04:18,370 --> 00:04:26,680
Gran Mari: Sunlight looks plain. But it is made of every color, all mixed up together.

40
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:31,970
Ollie: A rainbow! On the wall!

41
00:04:33,470 --> 00:04:42,060
Gran Mari: The water bends the light and spreads the colors apart. Tiny drops of rain work just like this glass.

42
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,910
Gus: So the rainbow is hiding in the sunlight?

43
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:49,520
Gran Mari: Well now, what do you think happens next?

44
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:56,050
Ollie: It moves if you move the glass!

45
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:04,620
Pip: It needs the sun to shine through!

46
00:05:12,550 --> 00:05:17,680
Ollie: Try it at home with a grown-up! Fill a clear glass with water. Set it on a sunny windowsill.

47
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:28,960
Ollie: Look at the wall nearby. Find the rainbow! Never look right at the sun.

48
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:39,680
Gus: Wait. I have to tell you something.

49
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:46,830
Gus: I said my rainbow was sleeping. That was a fib. I covered it with my hat.

50
00:05:48,330 --> 00:05:52,410
Gus: I wanted it all for me, and then it was gone. I'm sorry.

51
00:05:53,910 --> 00:05:58,460
Ollie: Thanks for telling us the truth, Gus.

52
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:11,290
Pip: Look! It's on my shell too!

53
00:06:13,070 --> 00:06:15,130
Bean: Share!

54
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:27,480
Gus: There's enough for everybody! That's the best part!

55
00:06:29,070 --> 00:06:31,400
Pip: It sparkles even more, with friends.

56
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:38,200
Ollie: Time for my Wonder Pocket! Three things we learned.

57
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:50,090
Ollie: One. Sunlight is made of all the colors.

58
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:55,380
Ollie: Two. Water bends the light and spreads the colors out.

59
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:02,630
Ollie: Three. A rainbow needs sunshine. It fades when it's hidden.

60
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:09,910
Ollie: And one kind thing to try today. Share your favorite thing.

61
00:07:11,410 --> 00:07:16,260
Gus: Bye, everybody! Next time, I'll share first!
